<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0C1134043003">
<title>
DTC Confirmation Procedure
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Check that the following condition is met in this “DTC Confirmation Procedure”.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
8.5 V &#60; battery &#60; 16 V
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Connect SUZUKI scan tool to DLC.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Display “ECT” of “Data List” mode on SUZUKI scan tool.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Race engine so that engine coolant temperature reaches 103 &#176;C (217 &#176;F) or more.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Stop engine.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Repeat Step 2) – 4) 2 times.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLSB0C1134043004">
<title>
DTC Troubleshooting
</title>
<diag type = "test" id = "AENLSB0C1134043005">
<testgroup id = "AENLSB0C1134043006">
<question>
Was “Engine and Emission Control System Check” performed?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to Step 2.
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0C1134001">Engine and Emission Control System Check:K12D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
<testgroup id = "AENLSB0C1134043007">
<title>
Radiator cooling fan relay No.2 and No.3 power supply circuit (coil side) check
</title>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “OFF”, remove radiator cooling fan relays No.2 and No.3.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check for proper terminal connection to radiator cooling fan relay No.2 and No.3 connectors.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
If connections are OK, set ignition “ON”.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check that voltage between each of “A2” and “A3” and ground is battery voltage.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<question>
Is check result OK?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to Step 3.
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Repair or replace defective wire harness.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
<testgroup id = "AENLSB0C1134043008">
<title>
Radiator cooling fan relay No.2 and No.3 check
</title>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check radiator cooling fan relays No.2 and No.3. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0C1636011"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</test1>
<question>
Is check result OK?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to Step 4.
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Replace radiator cooling fan relays No.2 and/or No.3.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
<testgroup id = "AENLSB0C1134043009">
<title>
Radiator cooling fan relay No.2 and No.3 drive circuit check
</title>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “OFF”, disconnect “C01” and “E01” connectors from ECM.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check for proper terminal connection to “C01” and “E01” connectors.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
If connections are OK, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance of “B2” circuit: less than 1 &#937;
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance between “B2” circuit and ground: infinity
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance between “B2” circuit terminal and other terminal at radiator cooling fan relay No.2 and No.3 connectors: infinity
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Voltage of “B2” circuit: approx. 0 V (When ignition is “ON”)
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</test1>
<question>
Is check result OK?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Replace ECM and recheck DTC. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0C1336001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Repair or replace defective wire harness.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
</diag>
